Package: lorps
Type: Package
Title: Low-Rank Probit Stick-Breaking Multiple Imputation
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Bhargob", "Kakoty",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "kakot001@umn.edu"),
    person("Thierry", "Chekouo",
           role = "aut"),
    person("Eric F.", "Lock",
           role = "aut")
    )
Description: Provides a Bayesian nonparametric approach to multiple imputation of
    missing values in high-dimensional data matrices. The method combines
    flexible mixture modeling with a low-rank structure to borrow information
    across rows and columns, allowing for complex data distributions while
    accounting for uncertainty in the missing values.
License: GPL-3
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports: Rcpp, RcppTN, parallel, parallelly, stats, utils
LinkingTo: Rcpp, RcppArmadillo (>= 14.6.0-1), RcppTN
Suggests: mitools
SystemRequirements: C++17
NeedsCompilation: yes
